{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "presets_version": "2.0.0",
  "min_claude_code": "2.1.0",
  "_doc": [
    "Claude Code evaluates deny -> ask -> allow and STOPS at the first match.",
    "Two consequences drive the shape of this file:",
    "",
    "1. An ask rule that is BROADER than an allow rule silently kills it.",
    "   Bash(git config:*) in ask would defeat Bash(git config --get:*) in allow.",
    "   Every ask entry here is narrower than the allow entry it qualifies.",
    "",
    "2. To restrict something, prefer REMOVING it from allow over adding it to",
    "   ask. Removing lets the command fall through to Claude Code's normal",
    "   prompt; adding to ask does the same thing but also survives",
    "   bypassPermissions mode. Use ask only when it must hold under bypass.",
    "",
    "deny is ignored under bypassPermissions; ask is not. Anything that must",
    "hold in bypass mode therefore belongs in ask, never deny."
  ],
  "global": {
    "_doc": [
      "Tier-independent. Tiers are a trust axis - 'I trust Claude more with my",
      "codebase' must never also mean 'I am willing to lose my AWS credentials'.",
      "Inheritance is monotonic, so a per-tier deny would give HIGHER trust MORE",
      "denies, which is backwards.",
      "",
      "These are the commands that were previously in _excluded_from_all_tiers,",
      "which no code ever read. Promoting them here is the whole point: they were",
      "documented as excluded while Bash(git push:*) auto-approved --force.",
      "",
      "Entries here mostly do NOT add prompts relative to 1.x: except for the",
      "rules listed in _newly_prompting, nothing here was ever in an allow array,",
      "so it already prompted. What changes is that the behaviour is now explicit,",
      "deterministic, and survives bypass mode."
    ],
    "_newly_prompting_doc": [
      "Rules that WERE auto-approved under a 1.x tier and now prompt. This is the",
      "CANDIDATE set; resolve_newly_prompting filters it against the user's actual",
      "previous allow list, because whether a rule loses auto-approval depends on",
      "what that user had.",
      "",
      "forge prints the filtered list and requires confirmation before applying -",
      "a count in a summary line is not consent. The 1.x forms were broad",
      "wildcards (Bash(gh:*), Bash(aws:*), Bash(docker compose:*)), never the",
      "narrow rules replacing them, so the match is by prefix coverage."
    ],
