    "full-autonomy": {
      "label": "Full Autonomy",
      "tier": 3,
      "description": "Claude runs development commands without asking. Still asks before destructive operations.",
      "detail": "Auto-approves: everything above, plus git, package managers, compilers, build tools, test runners, linters, Docker, and web access. You approve: rm, sudo, force pushes, hard resets, and anything that touches credentials.",
      "inherits": "auto-edit",
      "default_mode": "default",
      "_allow_doc": {
        "wrappers_removed": [
          "Bash(bash:*), Bash(sh:*), Bash(zsh:*), Bash(source:*), Bash(.:*) and",
          "Bash(./:*) are gone. A universal shell wrapper in an allow list voids",
          "every other rule in it.",
          "",
          "Bash(timeout:*), Bash(nohup:*), Bash(xargs:*) and Bash(command:*) are",
          "gone for a subtler reason: Claude Code already strips those wrappers",
          "before matching, so `timeout 5 npm test` still matches Bash(npm test:*).",
          "Keeping the wrapper rule bought nothing and allowed `timeout 5 rm -rf /`.",
          "xargs is special-cased too - a prefix rule matches `xargs <prefix>` on",
          "its own, so Bash(xargs:*) only ever added `xargs rm`."
        ],
        "git_c_removed": [
          "Bash(git -c:*) and Bash(git config:*) are removed.",
          "`git -c alias.x='!sh -c \"...\"' x` is arbitrary execution through an",
          "allowlisted prefix, and `git config alias.x '!cmd'` is the same attack",
          "with a persistent payload. Read forms stay allowed at tier 1.",
          "Bash(git -C:*) is kept - it is genuinely useful, and the wildcard ask",
          "rules (git * push --force*) cover the flag-in-the-middle forms."
        ],
        "compose": [
          "The hyphenated binary is a different command string and matched nothing",
          "in 1.x, so every docker-compose invocation prompted."
        ],
        "cloud": [
          "aws/gcloud/kubectl were Bash(aws:*)-style wildcards, which auto-approved",
          "credential exfiltration. Read verbs only now; mutating verbs are in",
          "global.ask."
        ],
        "gh": [
          "gh pr/issue/run are the everyday verbs and stay broad. Credential and",
          "delete verbs are in global.ask, including the `gh api` forms - gh api is",
          "a full authenticated client and would otherwise defeat every narrow rule."
        ],
        "interpreters": [
          "perl joins python3/node/ruby/php, which tier 3 already allowed with :*",
          "and which already accept -c/-e. Excluding only perl was incoherent, and",
          "it was the single largest allowlist gap measured (293 commands).",
          "",
          "This means tier 3 is 'Claude may run code', and the ask list is a",
          "guardrail on routine behaviour rather than a boundary against a",
          "determined prompt injection: any ask rule is one `perl -e 'system(...)'`",
          "away from being routed around. That is the honest description, and the",
          "README says so too."
        ]
      },
